# Task Sheet & Context-File Hygiene

Mirror of `.claude/rules/tasks.md`. Keep both in sync.

## Where tasks live

- `docs/tasks/index.md`: status tables and the prioritised **Next up** (top 5). Status and routing only.
- `docs/tasks/<ID>-<kebab-title>.md`: one task per file (facts, deliverables, TDD plan, BDD ACs, do/don't, verify).
- `docs/tasks/completed/`: task files moved here once verified done.
- `docs/tasks/PLAYBOOK.md`: how to execute any task. Read once per session.

## Rules

1. Start at the index; pick from Next up unless the user names a task. If the top item is not ready, surface the blocker.
2. Code change, task-file status/AC ticks, and the index row (with re-ordered Next up) land in **one commit**.
3. Done means verified: every AC checked against reality, gate green with output seen, user-facing behaviour checked in Chrome. Otherwise 🟡 Partial.
4. Re-order Next up on every status change.
5. Record deviations under the AC; record rejected options in the Decision log.
6. Re-verify `file:line` facts before acting; fix stale ones in the same commit.
7. Out-of-scope discoveries become a new task file + index row, not a TODO.

## Context-file size rule

Any file loaded to orient (task files, index, STATUS, PLAYBOOK, rules, agent instructions, CLAUDE.md, AGENTS.md, OPENCODE-DEV.md) past **400 lines** is split the next time it is touched: `index.md` (routing only) + per-section leaves, verbatim, verified by line counts, 5-line stub at the old path. Exempt: `docs/tasks/completed/`, `docs/reviews/`, `docs/requirements/`, `project-documentation/`, `sessions-memory/`.
